## Hints

- Part 1: monthly period index: `df.to_period("M")`; groupby-period
  agg; `.groupby(level=...)` per name then shift(1) the whole
  predictor block — shift AFTER aggregation, never before.
- Part 2: z-scoring per name: (s − s.mean())/s.std() on that name's
  time series. VIF of two z-scored regressors is the same number for
  every name — compute it from corr(z_vol, z_dv).
- Part 3: IQR-to-bp: mean slope × (IQR of z-scored vol = ~1.35 sigma)
  × 1e4; the anomaly literature's monthly effects are 30–100 bp/IQR.
- Part 4: sign agreement under pure noise is ~50%; above 65% starts
  meaning something at 50 names.
